**Convention 1.1 (mathematical domain).** This volume continues the original weak finite-activity problem of [FA, §§67–72, 77–79][FA] and [RC, §§58, 67–76][RC]. Its statements are ordinary conditional mathematics. The owning source definitions, isolated root and ranks are [CG, Definition 13.1, Proposition 13.2, Corollary 13.3 and Theorem 15.1][CG]; the full stopped-output minimax statement is CG Theorems 14.1, 15.2 and 16.1. CG Theorem 17.2 identifies the sign-averaged live Choi matrix and its stated pre-average support consequences. It does not identify every unaveraged complete channel. The sharp joint acquisition cost and the unaveraged supported real equality face are supplied separately by [JR, Theorems 37.2 and 42.1][JR]. The actual-label reduction, fractional capacities and admitted time-law scope are FA Theorems 69.1–69.2 and 72.1, with RC Convention 67.1 and Proposition 75.1. These source-root, minimax, sharp-cost and full-class antecedents remain `ASSUMED-UNVERIFIED` as antecedents of this volume; the additional interval theorem does not recertify them. All physical operator equalities hold at their same true consistent source point. Rectangular enclosures bound expressions and root systems; unrelated points in those rectangles are not asserted to be normalized physical sources.

